test_validity -- the mesh checks del_vor makes before any geometry (Nov 2026)
=======================================================================

QUICK START

  sh run_validity_tests.sh [path-to-del_vor]   17 runs, under 1 s
  open summary.html

WHAT IS TESTED

  For each mesh made by make_validity_inputs.py (one per line of
  cases.txt):

  del_vor -avs NAME.inp -stor NAME.stor -report NAME.report

  Eleven meshes each break one rule; each is a fatal error:

  mixed, quad, missing_vertex      cell types: all triangles or all
                                   tets, vertices that exist
  inverted, flat_tet,              cells of positive size (tet volume
  repeat_vertex, flat_tri          in LaGriT's vertex order, triangle
                                   area)
  face_in_3_tets, edge_in_3_tris   conformity: a tet face in at most 2
                                   tets, a triangle edge in at most 2
                                   triangles of one itetclr
  flipped_tri, moebius             orientation: neighboring triangles
                                   of one itetclr run along their
                                   shared edge in opposite directions

  Six are legal meshes that look unusual and must run to the end:
  two_fractures (two itetclr crossing along one edge), clockwise
  (every triangle clockwise), unused_vertex (a WARNING),
  two_materials (a material interface between two tets) and
  wrapped_attr (vertex data running onto a second line, as LaGriT
  writes it) and odd_text (CR LF line ends, tabs, Fortran D
  exponents: its .stor must equal two_materials's).

WHAT IS CHECKED (check_validity.py)

  exit      the exit status cases.txt expects (1 or 0)
  message   the expected text is in the screen output
  files     a failed run wrote no .stor and no violations file; a
            passing run wrote its .stor
  same_as   odd_text's .stor equals two_materials's (date line aside)

PICTURES (logs/)

  NAME.svg  every cell's edges, vertex numbers, itetclr 2 in blue,
            the cells the message names as "first" filled red

FILES

  run_validity_tests.sh     runner (work/, logs/)
  make_validity_inputs.py   the 17 meshes
  check_validity.py         checks, pictures, summary.html
  cases.txt                 name | exit | message | what it does
